# motoquencer2 RAM accounting (manual/circuits/experimental/motoquencer2.md:
# ram_bytes 1188 — motoquencer's 1184 plus 4 for the resolved probability mode; the
# notch tables themselves are constant data, not per-circuit RAM).
# Hand-computed Forge accounting on a MASTER (typeOfMaster()==16 always adds the
# X7's 864 bytes, attached or not):
#   x7                            864
#   m4                            312
#   motoquencer2 base            1188
#   clock = I1 (taptempo input)    40
#   cv    = O1 (output)             4
#   constants                      16   (seeded {0.0, 1.0} = 8 -> ALIGN_UP(8,16))
#   ----------------------------------
#   total                        2424
# The same lines under [motoquencer] cost 2420 (ram-vs-motoquencer.gold): the two
# circuits differ by exactly the 4-byte base delta. Patching `probabilitymode = 2`
# would add 8 bytes (a simple input that is not 0 or 1).
experimental
expect_ram 2424
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer2]
    clock = I1
    cv    = O1
>>>
@0 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
